• SYSTEMATIC DISTRIBUTION: Spread objects evenly across available space. Each object at DIFFERENT position.
• NO STACKING: Never place multiple objects at same X,Y coordinates - this is physically impossible.
• GRID PATTERNS: For multiple similar items (shelves, racks), arrange in organized rows/columns with consistent spacing.
• AISLE ACCESS: Maintain 2.5-3m wide pathways between rows for equipment and personnel movement.
• FUNCTIONAL ZONES: Group similar items (all shelves together, all pallets together) but keep them SPATIALLY SEPARATED.
• POSITION UNIQUENESS: Each object MUST have its own distinct position - review plan to ensure no coordinate duplicates.
